---
layout: layouts/piece.njk
title: "The Café — Closed Post (1080 × 1350)"
canvasW: "1080px"
canvasH: "1350px"
pageCss: "/assets/css/studio/fb-closed.css"

# The closure. The caption (fb-closed.11tydata.js) reads these same fields, so
# the picture and the words can't disagree. For another holiday, change these
# and the studio lines below; empty `thanks` leaves that line out. The website
# and /reserve read site.json's closedDays, so add the day there too.
closedDate: "2026-11-11"
holiday: "Veterans Day"
backDate: "2026-11-12"
thanks: "Thank you to everyone who has served."

tags: studio
studioWeekly: true
studioTitle: "Closed for Veterans Day — Facebook post"
studioCategory: "Social"
studioSize: "1080 × 1350 px · portrait feed post"
studioNote: "We're closed Wednesday, November 11 for Veterans Day, back Thursday, November 12 (client 2026-10-31). The day, the holiday and the thank-you are in this piece's front matter, and the caption is built from them. Change them for the next holiday closure."
studioW: 1080
studioH: 1350
studioOrder: 25
---
{#- One message: the day we're closed and the day we're back.

    A cream body between the teal bands, so the red can be read (never red on
    teal). The red, teal and cream with the stars are all the holiday styling
    it needs: no flag, no emoji.

    Every size is set for the ~540px a portrait post shows at on a phone:
    nothing a customer needs is under 24px. -#}
{%- set o = site.opening %}
{%- set opens = (o.opens.time | replace(":00", "")) + o.opens.meridiem %}
{%- set closes = (o.closes.time | replace(":00", "")) + o.closes.meridiem %}
{%- set star = "50,2 60.8,35.2 95.6,35.2 67.4,55.7 78.2,88.8 50,68.3 21.8,88.8 32.6,55.7 4.4,35.2 39.2,35.2" %}
<div class="canvas fc">

    <header class="fc-head">
        <div class="wordmark wordmark--light wordmark--hero fc-wordmark">
            {% inlineSvg "/assets/thecafe.svg", "", site.name %}
        </div>
        <p class="p-display-italic fc-kicker">{{ holiday }}</p>
        <p class="p-label fc-range">{{ site.address.locality }}, {{ site.address.region }}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="fc-body">
        <h1 class="p-display fc-headline">We&rsquo;re closed</h1>
        <p class="p-display fc-date">{{ closedDate | dayDate("long") }}</p>

        <div class="fc-stars" aria-hidden="true">
            {%- for size in ["side", "mid", "side"] %}
            <svg class="fc-star fc-star--{{ size }}" viewBox="0 0 100 100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><polygon points="{{ star }}"/></svg>
            {%- endfor %}
        </div>

        {%- if thanks %}
        <p class="p-display-italic fc-thanks">{{ thanks }}</p>
        {%- endif %}

        <div class="fc-back">
            <p class="p-label fc-back-label">We&rsquo;ll be back</p>
            <p class="p-display fc-back-day">{{ backDate | dayDate("long") }} at {{ opens }}</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <footer class="fc-foot">
        <p class="p-display fc-foot-call">{{ site.phone }} <span class="dot">&middot;</span> {{ site.social.website }}</p>
        <p class="p-body fc-foot-line">{{ o.hoursDays }}, {{ opens }} &ndash; {{ closes }} &middot; {{ site.address.street }}, {{ site.address.locality }}, {{ site.address.region }}</p>
    </footer>

</div>
